# Several files in this repository are *delivered to a router* and executed by
# busybox ash (tools/router/mt7603u.init is copied to /etc/init.d/, the .sh
# helpers are piped into `sh -s`).  On a Windows checkout with the usual
# core.autocrlf=true they would come out with CRLF, and the first line then
# fails with `not found` -- a confusing failure far from its cause.
#
# So: keep LF in the repository *and* in every checkout, whatever autocrlf says.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.init     text eol=lf
*.mk       text eol=lf
Makefile   text eol=lf
*.c        text eol=lf
*.h        text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
